cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its analyses, please cite the version you used. Version DOIs are listed on the Zenodo record; the earlier versions are identified below."
type: software
title: "Tessera-ST: a gated graph encoder for spatial omics and its controls audit"
authors:
  - family-names: Fu
    given-names: Zeyu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-8329-0108"
version: "2026.11.05-revision-r1"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23992778"
date-released: "2026-11-05"
license: MIT
abstract: "Tessera-ST is a self-supervised gated graph encoder for spatial molecular data (earlier releases call it Tessera). This release contains the evaluated implementation, the controls audit of the original submission, and the analyses added during review: training budget, patient-excluded tuning of the encoder, cluster number with fixed representations, and native external methods, together with their protocol, tests and result tables. Third-party data, annotations and images retain their source-specific terms."
identifiers:
